        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.107,
            0.64,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Find 6 rational numbers between 3 and 4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.137,
            0.641,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Find 5 rational numbers between "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.185,
            0.635,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Find 5 rational numbers between "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 6 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.222,
            0.633,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{x}{3} + \\frac{x}{5} = \\frac{16}{15}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , find the rational number x."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.267,
            0.883,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Let a and b be two non-zero rational numbers such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a   +   { \\frac { 1 } { b } }   =   0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Without assigning any numerical values, determine whether ab is positive or negative. Justify your answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.352,
            0.886,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. A rational number has a terminating decimal expansion whose last non-zero digit occurs in the 4th decimal place. Show that such a number can be written in the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { p } { 1 0 ^ { 4 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is an integer not divisible by 10. Is it necessary that the denominator of this rational number, when written in the lowest form, is divisible by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ^ { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 ^ { 4 } \\sharp"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Give reasons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.494,
            0.886,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. Without performing division, determine whether the decimal expansion of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 8 } { 1 2 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is terminating or non-terminating. If it terminates, state the number of decimal places."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.576,
            0.885,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. A rational number in its lowest form has denominator "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ^ { 3 } \\times 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . How many decimal places will its decimal expansion have? Explain your answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.648,
            0.885,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*13. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = { \\frac { 7 } { 1 2 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b = \\frac{5}{6}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Express both a and b in the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { k _ { 1 } } { m }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { k _ { 2 } } { m }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "k _ { \\mathrm { { } _ { 1 } } } ,   k _ { \\mathrm { { } _ { 2 } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and m are integers and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "k _ { _ 2 } - k _ { _ 1 } > 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Using the same denominator m, write exactly five distinct rational numbers lying between a and b keeping an integer numerator. Explain why the condition "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "k_{2}-k_{1}>n+1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is necessary to find n such rational numbers between the two rational numbers a and b using this method."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.811,
            0.885,
            0.875
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*14. Three rational numbers x, y, z satisfy "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x + y + z = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "xy + yz + zx = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Show that all the rational numbers "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x , y , z"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " must be simultaneously zero."
            }
          ]
        }
